Installation
------------

macOS (Apple Silicon + Intel, macOS 12 or later)
  - Audio Unit: copy PhaseScope.component to ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/
  - VST3:       copy PhaseScope.vst3      to ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/
  - Standalone: copy PhaseScope.app       to /Applications/
  - The builds are not notarized. Remove the quarantine flag once in Terminal:
      xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/PhaseScope.component
      xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/PhaseScope.vst3
  - Restart your DAW (Logic: Plug-in Manager -> Reset & Rescan if needed).

Windows (64-bit)
  - VST3: copy the PhaseScope.vst3 folder to C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3\
  - Standalone: run PhaseScope.exe. The build is not code-signed, so Windows
    SmartScreen may warn on first start ("More info" -> "Run anyway").
  - Let your DAW rescan its plugins.


Usage
-----

Insert PhaseScope as the last plugin on the master bus (after the limiter) so
it measures what is actually played back.


